We designed a survey based on the PIECES framework and asked participants to rate their experience with INSUS on a Likert scale. The Likert scale is a widely used rating scale in social science research that measures attitudes or perceptions on a continuum from strongly agree to strongly disagree. We used a ﬁve-point Likert scale, where 1 indicated “strongly disagree” and 5 indicated “strongly agree”.

